   "subject": "Bootstrapping rsquare in a multi-group model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I am looking to bootstrap the r2 value of a three group multi-group path model so that I can then compare them across groups.<div><br></div><div>I can get the r2 values using inspect such as:<br><div><br></div><div><div>g1.r2.y &lt;- inspect(fit, &#39;r2&#39;)$`1`[[1]]</div><div><br></div><div>g2.r2.y &lt;- inspect(fit, &#39;r2&#39;)$`2`[[1]]</div><div><br></div><div>g3.r2.y &lt;- inspect(fit, &#39;r2&#39;)$`3`[[1]]</div></div></div><div><br></div><div>But I&#39;m not sure how to set up the bootstrapLavaan for example:</div><div><br></div><div>bootstraoLavaan(g1.r2.y, R=10, type=&quot;ordinary&quot;, FUN = &quot;coef&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>Has anyone done this before and able to offer suggestions on how to make this work? My goal is to compare the 3 r-square values across groups to test if they are significantly different.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,<br><br>Scott</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c-3DLyejAQAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2020-04-09T23:45:40Z",
   "subject": "Re: Bootstrapping rsquare in a multi-group model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">As the help page shows (see <b>Details</b>), you need to define your own function that returns what you want, and pass that to the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> FUN= </font>argument.<div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">myFunc </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span></div></code></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  g1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inspect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;r2&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$</span><span style=\"color:#080\">`1`</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  g2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inspect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;r2&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$</span><span style=\"color:#080\">`2`</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>  g3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inspect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;r2&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$</span><span style=\"color:#080\">`3`</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span></div></code></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">## calculate differences</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g12 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    g13 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    g23 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">out</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bootstrapLavaan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> R</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ordinary&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FUN </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> myFunc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><div><br></div><div>Look at<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> str(out) </font>to see its structure (you will get a bootstrap distribution of each statistic your function returns).  Then you can write code to calculate your 95% percentile CI, for example:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">apply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">out</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> quantile</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> probs </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">025</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">975</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422102943000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0oyv-dYMcFSTydRaz5dQ0b\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
